PROOF ORDER
  1. Relation-support axis: split support-2 cut terms, support-3 Schur
     packets, and higher support; do not expect reverse-pair cancellation.
  2. Factorial-support axis: on the high-height/nonresonant tail, prove
     an odd-L1 envelope for W_1+W_3+W_5 versus W_0+W_2+W_4+W_6.
  3. Route finite_even_L1_ledger rows and signed-even-led packets through
     the HYP-2717/HYP-2714 low-height ledger.
  4. Only after those filters evaluate Q0=even_support-odd_support.

SYNTHESIS
  Odd support remains useful only on the factorial axis, as an L1
  envelope.  On the relation-lattice axis, parity is a false friend;
  support size, especially support-3 Schur packets, is the live geometry.
